<speak>Exactly. We had that problem with our travel papers recently. I saved them under the name of the city, while my wife looked under the airline. Neither of us was wrong, but we were both convinced the other had lost the document. Now we put a short description in the filename. I don't need a sophisticated system, just something I can still follow when I'm tired. After a long day at the business, even a very clever folder structure can feel like a puzzle.</speak>